          "rule_title": "Process Execution From Shared Memory Directory",
          "rule_description": "Detects the execution of a binary from the Linux shared memory directory /dev/shm.\nThis directory is a tmpfs mount backed entirely by RAM and is abused by attackers for fileless malware staging because files written there never touch physical disk and may evade disk-based detection.\n",
